{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QksKZ89KUWwajqpt1VAbkW","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds a starter lint scanner role (golangci-lint per Go module plus `//nolint` directives, minus a human-owned baseline) so repos can file lint findings beyond a committed baseline. It fails closed on anything that would make findings vanish and autoclose.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/roles/scanners/lint/`: `scan` (POSIX sh, 0755, forced golangci-lint flags, `--baseline` mode, exit codes 0/1/2), `normalize.jq` (fingerprints, collapse, severity, fenced untrusted text, baseline parsing, three modes) and a pinned `Dockerfile`.\n- `internal/roles/testdata/lint/`: 15 synthetic cases, 3 real cases (`basic`, `nested_module`, `repo_config_new_only`) and `regen.sh`.\n- `internal/roles/lint_test.go`, `lint_scan_test.go`: golden, case-list, decode and untrusted-text tests, and a stubbed end-to-end scan test (argv, exit codes, read-only repo).\n- `lint_integration_test.go`, `lint_docker_integration_test.go` (tag `integration`); `scanRunArgs` doc comment generalised.\n- `config.yaml`: `scanners/lint` override and four `**/.golangci.*` protected paths. `roles.go` embeds `scanners/lint`.\n- `initcmd/body.go`: baseline bullet in the init PR body. Tests updated in `roles_test.go` and `initcmd_test.go`.\n- `Makefile`: `lint-scanner-fixtures`. Docs: `docs/proposal.md` (table, \"The lint scanner\", init and protected-path text) and `docs/layout.md`.\n\n## Testing\n- `go test ./...`: all pass. `go vet ./...` and `go vet -tags integration ./internal/roles/`: clean. Changed Go files are gofmt-clean.\n- `go test -tags integration -run TestIntegrationLintHost ./internal/roles/` passes with the host's golangci-lint 2.15.0.\n- The three real fixture cases were generated by running `regen.sh` with the host's golangci-lint 2.15.0, not hand-built.\n\n## Open issues\n- Not run here: the Docker integration test and `make lint-scanner-fixtures`. The Dockerfile pins were copied from the cve Dockerfile and are marked \"verification pending human\" in its header. A human must build the image and rerun the fixtures before merge.\n- `make lint` reports a gofmt error in `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`. That file is unchanged by this PR.\n- The plan named CLAUDE.md, but its Layout section now points to `docs/layout.md`, so that file was updated instead.\n- Not wired: enabling the scanner in this repo's own `.ard/` (with its baseline) and the follow-up issues stay with a maintainer.\n#!/bin/sh\n# lint scanner: lint findings beyond a committed baseline, as ard findings.\n#\n# Contract (see docs/proposal.md, Scanners):\n#   - cwd is a read-only worktree of origin/main. This script finds its siblings\n#     (normalize.jq, baseline, golangci.yml) from its own path, never from cwd.\n#   - Prints findings as JSON lines on stdout, and only as its very last action:\n#     any failure exits non-zero with nothing on stdout, and the controller\n#     discards the run. It never prints partial results.\n#   - Writes nothing outside a mktemp dir that is removed on exit. HOME may be\n#     unwritable. It holds no GitHub token and needs none.\n#   - stderr is the job log: tool versions, one line per Go module, final counts.\n#\n# What it does: runs golangci-lint v2 once per go.mod (the repo's own config, or\n# ./golangci.yml next to this script when that human-owned file exists), lists\n# every //nolint directive in .go files, and drops findings whose fingerprint is\n# in the human-owned ./baseline file. A missing baseline fails the run: commit an\n# empty file to mean \"no baseline\".\n#\n# Arguments: none, or exactly --baseline, which prints a baseline of ALL current\n# findings (ignoring ./baseline, not requiring it): scan --baseline > baseline.\n#\n# The golangci-lint flags below are forced after any config, so a repo config\n# cannot truncate output or report \"new issues only\": either would make findings\n# vanish and be autoclosed. Go only, with the image's Go (GOTOOLCHAIN=local).\n#\n# Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 a required tool is missing.\nset -eu\n\ndir=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\n\ndie() { echo \"lint: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }\nneed() { command -v \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"lint: $1 not found\" >&2; exit 2; }; }\n\nmode=findings\ncase $# in\n  0) ;;\n  1) if [ \"$1\" = \"--baseline\" ]; then mode=baseline; else echo \"usage: scan [--baseline]\" >&2; exit 1; fi ;;\n  *) echo \"usage: scan [--baseline]\" >&2; exit 1 ;;\nesac\n\nneed golangci-lint\nneed go\nneed jq\nneed find\nneed grep\n\ntmp=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/ard-lint.XXXXXX\")\n# Go's module cache is read-only on disk; make it removable first.\ncleanup() { chmod -R u+w \"$tmp\" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf \"$tmp\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT\ntrap 'exit 130' INT\ntrap 'exit 143' TERM\n\n# Keep Go's caches off an unwritable HOME and out of the worktree.\nfor v in GOCACHE GOMODCACHE GOPATH; do\n  eval \"cur=\\${$v:-}\"\n  if [ -z \"$cur\" ] || [ ! -w \"$cur\" ]; then\n    eval \"$v=\\$tmp/$v; export $v\"\n  fi\ndone\nGOLANGCI_LINT_CACHE=$tmp/golangci\nGOWORK=off GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly GOTOOLCHAIN=local\nexport GOLANGCI_LINT_CACHE GOWORK GOFLAGS GOTOOLCHAIN\n\nversion=$(golangci-lint version --short 2>/dev/null || golangci-lint --version | head -n 1) || version=unknown\necho \"golangci-lint: $version\" >&2\necho \"go: $(go env GOVERSION)\" >&2\n\nif [ \"$mode\" = findings ]; then\n  [ -f \"$dir/baseline\" ] || die 'no baseline file: generate one with \"scan --baseline > baseline\" in the role directory and commit it (an empty file means no baseline)'\n  baseline=$dir/baseline\nelse\n  : > \"$tmp/empty\"\n  baseline=$tmp/empty\nfi\n\ncfg=\nif [ -f \"$dir/golangci.yml\" ]; then\n  cfg=\"--config $dir/golangci.yml\"\n  echo \"golangci: using role config\" >&2\nelse\n  echo \"golangci: repo config or defaults\" >&2\nfi\n\nprune='( -name .git -o -name vendor -o -name node_modules -o -name testdata ) -prune'\n\n# golangci-lint, once per Go module. Fail closed: a module that cannot be\n# analysed fails the run.\n: > \"$tmp/gl.jsonl\"\nfind . $prune -o -name go.mod -type f -print > \"$tmp/mods.raw\" || die \"find failed\"\nLC_ALL=C sort \"$tmp/mods.raw\" > \"$tmp/mods.txt\"\nn=0\nwhile IFS= read -r f; do\n  manifest=${f#./}\n  mdir=$(dirname -- \"$manifest\")\n  n=$((n + 1))\n  rc=0\n  # $cfg is intentionally unquoted: it is empty or two words.\n  # shellcheck disable=SC2086\n  (cd -- \"$mdir\" && golangci-lint run $cfg \\\n    --path-mode=abs --output.json.path=\"$tmp/$n.json\" --output.text.path=stderr \\\n    --show-stats=false --issues-exit-code=0 --max-issues-per-linter=0 --max-same-issues=0 \\\n    --new=false --new-from-rev= --new-from-merge-base= --new-from-patch= \\\n    --fix=false --allow-parallel-runners ./...) 2>\"$tmp/gl.err\" || rc=$?\n  if [ \"$rc\" -ne 0 ]; then\n    if grep -qi 'go version\\|requires go\\|toolchain' \"$tmp/gl.err\"; then\n      tail -n 3 \"$tmp/gl.err\" >&2\n      die \"$manifest needs a newer Go than the image's $(go env GOVERSION); update the lint image\"\n    fi\n    die \"golangci-lint failed in $manifest (exit $rc): $(tail -n 3 \"$tmp/gl.err\")\"\n  fi\n  [ -s \"$tmp/$n.json\" ] || die \"golangci-lint wrote no report for $manifest\"\n  jq -c --arg module \"$mdir\" '{module: $module, report: .}' \"$tmp/$n.json\" >> \"$tmp/gl.jsonl\" \\\n    || die \"cannot parse golangci-lint output for $manifest\"\n  echo \"golangci-lint: $manifest: $(jq '(.Issues // []) | length' \"$tmp/$n.json\") issue(s)\" >&2\ndone < \"$tmp/mods.txt\"\n\n# //nolint directives are findings: they hide linter output.\n: > \"$tmp/nolint.jsonl\"\nrc=0\nfind . $prune -o -name '*.go' -type f -exec grep -lE '//[[:space:]]*nolint' {} + > \"$tmp/nolint.files\" || rc=$?\n[ \"$rc\" -le 1 ] || die \"searching for nolint directives failed\"\nLC_ALL=C sort \"$tmp/nolint.files\" > \"$tmp/nolint.sorted\"\nwhile IFS= read -r f; do\n  grep -nE '//[[:space:]]*nolint' \"$f\" \\\n    | jq -R -c --arg path \"${f#./}\" 'capture(\"^(?<line>[0-9]+):(?<text>.*)$\") | {path: $path, line: (.line|tonumber), text}' \\\n    >> \"$tmp/nolint.jsonl\" || die \"cannot read nolint directives in $f\"\ndone < \"$tmp/nolint.sorted\"\n\n# Merge. golangci-lint (--path-mode=abs) uses absolute paths; strip either root.\nroot=$(pwd -P)\nlroot=$(pwd)\nrun_jq() {\n  jq -n \"$1\" --arg mode \"$2\" --arg root \"$root\" --arg lroot \"$lroot\" --arg version \"$version\" \\\n    --rawfile baseline \"$baseline\" --slurpfile gl \"$tmp/gl.jsonl\" --slurpfile nolint \"$tmp/nolint.jsonl\" \\\n    -f \"$dir/normalize.jq\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$mode\" = baseline ]; then\n  run_jq -r baseline > \"$tmp/out\" || die \"normalize failed\"\n  echo \"lint: baseline written\" >&2\n  cat \"$tmp/out\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n\nrun_jq -c findings > \"$tmp/out\" || die \"normalize failed\"\nrun_jq -r fingerprints > \"$tmp/fps.raw\" || die \"normalize failed\"\nLC_ALL=C sort -u \"$tmp/fps.raw\" > \"$tmp/fps\"\nsed -e 's/\\r$//' -e 's/^[[:space:]]*//' -e 's/[[:space:]]*$//' \"$baseline\" \\\n  | grep -v -e '^#' -e '^$' | LC_ALL=C sort -u > \"$tmp/base\" || true\ncount=$(wc -l < \"$tmp/out\" | tr -d ' ')\nbaselined=$(LC_ALL=C comm -12 \"$tmp/fps\" \"$tmp/base\" | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\nunused=$(LC_ALL=C comm -13 \"$tmp/fps\" \"$tmp/base\" | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\necho \"lint: $count finding(s), $baselined baselined, $unused baseline entries unused\" >&2\ncat \"$tmp/out\"\ndiff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile\nindex 1dd6ab8..7c4f294 100644\n--- a/Makefile\n+++ b/Makefile\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n VERSION ?= $(shell git describe --tags --always --dirty 2>/dev/null || echo dev)\n LDFLAGS := -s -w -X main.version=$(VERSION)\n \n-.PHONY: build test lint fmt clean cve-fixtures chart-test image-test\n+.PHONY: build test lint fmt clean cve-fixtures lint-scanner-fixtures chart-test image-test\n \n build:\n \tCGO_ENABLED=0 go build -ldflags \"$(LDFLAGS)\" -o bin/ard ./cmd/ard\n@@ -33,5 +33,12 @@ cve-fixtures:\n \tdocker run --rm --user \"$$(id -u):$$(id -g)\" -e HOME=/tmp \\\n \t  -v \"$$PWD/internal/roles:/roles\" -w /roles ard-cve-fixtures sh testdata/cve/regen.sh\n \n+# Regenerates the real lint scanner fixtures in the pinned image (see\n+# internal/roles/testdata/lint/regen.sh). Needs Docker; not part of `make test`.\n+lint-scanner-fixtures:\n+\tdocker build -t ard-lint-fixtures internal/roles/scanners/lint\n+\tdocker run --rm --user \"$$(id -u):$$(id -g)\" -e HOME=/tmp \\\n+\t  -v \"$$PWD/internal/roles:/roles\" -w /roles ard-lint-fixtures sh testdata/lint/regen.sh\n+\n clean:\n \trm -rf bin\ndiff --git a/internal/initcmd/body.go b/internal/initcmd/body.go\nindex b9fea42..dab52be 100644\n--- a/internal/initcmd/body.go\n+++ b/internal/initcmd/body.go\n@@ -30,6 +30,12 @@ func initBody(ops []op, res *config.Resolved) string {\n \tb.WriteString(\"\\n## Before you merge\\n\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"- Nothing takes effect until this is merged: ard serve reads its configuration from origin/main.\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"- Merge with **Squash and merge** (recommended); **Create a merge commit** is also safe. Never fast-forward this branch into main from the command line: the bot-commit check reads main's first-parent history and would fail on the bot's commit.\\n\")\n+\tfor _, o := range ops {\n+\t\tif o.File.Path == \".ard/scanners/lint/scan\" {\n+\t\t\tb.WriteString(\"- The lint scanner fails until you commit `.ard/scanners/lint/baseline`: run the command in `.ard/scanners/lint/Dockerfile`'s header (an empty file means no baseline).\\n\")\n+\t\t\tbreak\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n \tb.WriteString(\"\\n## Follow-up the App cannot do\\n\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"ard's GitHub App has no permission to write `.github/`, so do this by hand:\\n\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"1. Copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` from the ard repository into this repository.\\n\")\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/config.yaml b/internal/roles/config.yaml\nindex a72acd4..702e494 100644\n--- a/internal/roles/config.yaml\n+++ b/internal/roles/config.yaml\n@@ -25,11 +25,18 @@ merge:\n     - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n     - .claude/\n     - .mcp.json\n+    # Linter config a PR could weaken: disabling a linter silently autocloses its issues.\n+    - \"**/.golangci.yml\"\n+    - \"**/.golangci.yaml\"\n+    - \"**/.golangci.toml\"\n+    - \"**/.golangci.json\"\n \n overrides:\n   scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n   scanners/docs: { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n   scanners/error-codes: { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n+  # needs a human-made `baseline` next to `scan`; see its Dockerfile\n+  scanners/lint: { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n   triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n   triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n   # timeout covers the whole worker job (agent, tests, fix rounds). tests is your\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/roles.go b/internal/roles/roles.go\nindex 7f2526f..74cc7c7 100644\n--- a/internal/roles/roles.go\n+++ b/internal/roles/roles.go\n@@ -7,11 +7,11 @@ package roles\n import \"embed\"\n \n // FS is the starter .ard/ tree `ard init` proposes: config.yaml plus the role\n-// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review and reviewers/security-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n+// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, scanners/lint, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review and reviewers/security-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n //\n // scanners/missing-tests is left out until its scan driver exists; re-add it when wiring it in.\n //\n-//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners/cve scanners/docs scanners/error-codes triage workers\n+//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners/cve scanners/docs scanners/error-codes scanners/lint triage workers\n var FS embed.FS\n \n // ExecutableNames lists base names that must be written 0755.\n .../roles/testdata/lint/digits_normalized/gl.jsonl |   1 +\n .../testdata/lint/digits_normalized/nolint.jsonl   |   0\n .../testdata/lint/digits_normalized/want.jsonl     |   1 +\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/empty/baseline        |   0\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/empty/gl.jsonl        |   1 +\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/empty/nolint.jsonl    |   0\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/empty/want.jsonl      |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/fingerprints_mode/baseline |   1 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/fingerprints_mode/gl.jsonl |   1 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/fingerprints_mode/mode     |   1 +\n .../testdata/lint/fingerprints_mode/nolint.jsonl   |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/fingerprints_mode/want.txt |   2 +\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/long_message/baseline |   0\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/long_message/gl.jsonl |   1 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/long_message/nolint.jsonl  |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/long_message/want.jsonl    |   2 +\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/many_lines/baseline   |   0\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/many_lines/gl.jsonl   |   1 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/many_lines/nolint.jsonl    |   0\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/many_lines/want.jsonl |   1 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/nested_module/baseline     |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/nested_module/gl.jsonl     |   2 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/nested_module/nolint.jsonl |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/nested_module/want.jsonl   |   8 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/nolint_directives/baseline |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/nolint_directives/gl.jsonl |   1 +\n .../testdata/lint/nolint_directives/nolint.jsonl   |   4 +\n .../testdata/lint/nolint_directives/want.jsonl     |   3 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/path_outside_root/baseline |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/path_outside_root/gl.jsonl |   1 +\n .../testdata/lint/path_outside_root/nolint.jsonl   |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/path_outside_root/want.err |   1 +\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/regen.sh              | 115 ++++++++\n .../testdata/lint/repo_config_new_only/baseline    |   0\n .../testdata/lint/repo_config_new_only/gl.jsonl    |   1 +\n .../lint/repo_config_new_only/nolint.jsonl         |   0\n .../testdata/lint/repo_config_new_only/want.jsonl  |   4 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/severity_table/baseline    |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/severity_table/gl.jsonl    |   1 +\n .../testdata/lint/severity_table/nolint.jsonl      |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/severity_table/want.jsonl  |  12 +\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/typecheck/baseline    |   0\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/typecheck/gl.jsonl    |   1 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/typecheck/nolint.jsonl     |   0\n internal/roles/testdata/lint/typecheck/want.err    |   1 +\n .../roles/testdata/lint/untrusted_text/baseline    |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/untrusted_text/gl.jsonl    |   1 +\n .../testdata/lint/untrusted_text/nolint.jsonl      |   0\n .../roles/testdata/lint/untrusted_text/want.jsonl  |   1 +\n 94 files changed, 1663 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4ee8848-b500-4ea0-8f2c-166d3ee04bc9","uuid":"f7d27f84-b565-432d-9c48-261c6bdc3cbf","timestamp":"2026-11-23T21:36:01.762Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds a starter lint scanner role (golangci-lint per Go module plus `//nolint` directives, minus a human-owned baseline) so repos can file lint findings beyond a committed baseline. It fails closed on anything that would make findings vanish and autoclose.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/roles/scanners/lint/`: `scan` (POSIX sh, 0755, forced golangci-lint flags, `--baseline` mode, exit codes 0/1/2), `normalize.jq` (fingerprints, collapse, severity, fenced untrusted text, baseline parsing, three modes) and a pinned `Dockerfile`.\n- `internal/roles/testdata/lint/`: 15 synthetic cases, 3 real cases (`basic`, `nested_module`, `repo_config_new_only`) and `regen.sh`.\n- `internal/roles/lint_test.go`, `lint_scan_test.go`: golden, case-list, decode and untrusted-text tests, and a stubbed end-to-end scan test (argv, exit codes, read-only repo).\n- `lint_integration_test.go`, `lint_docker_integration_test.go` (tag `integration`); `scanRunArgs` doc comment generalised.\n- `config.yaml`: `scanners/lint` override and four `**/.golangci.*` protected paths. `roles.go` embeds `scanners/lint`.\n- `initcmd/body.go`: baseline bullet in the init PR body. Tests updated in `roles_test.go` and `initcmd_test.go`.\n- `Makefile`: `lint-scanner-fixtures`. Docs: `docs/proposal.md` (table, \"The lint scanner\", init and protected-path text) and `docs/layout.md`.\n\n## Testing\n- `go test ./...`: all pass. `go vet ./...` and `go vet -tags integration ./internal/roles/`: clean. Changed Go files are gofmt-clean.\n- `go test -tags integration -run TestIntegrationLintHost ./internal/roles/` passes with the host's golangci-lint 2.15.0.\n- The three real fixture cases were generated by running `regen.sh` with the host's golangci-lint 2.15.0, not hand-built.\n\n## Open issues\n- Not run here: the Docker integration test and `make lint-scanner-fixtures`. The Dockerfile pins were copied from the cve Dockerfile and are marked \"verification pending human\" in its header. A human must build the image and rerun the fixtures before merge.\n- `make lint` reports a gofmt error in `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`. That file is unchanged by this PR.\n- The plan named CLAUDE.md, but its Layout section now points to `docs/layout.md`, so that file was updated instead.\n- Not wired: enabling the scanner in this repo's own `.ard/` (with its baseline) and the follow-up issues stay with a maintainer.\n#!/bin/sh\n# lint scanner: lint findings beyond a committed baseline, as ard findings.\n#\n# Contract (see docs/proposal.md, Scanners):\n#   - cwd is a read-only worktree of origin/main. This script finds its siblings\n#     (normalize.jq, baseline, golangci.yml) from its own path, never from cwd.\n#   - Prints findings as JSON lines on stdout, and only as its very last action:\n#     any failure exits non-zero with nothing on stdout, and the controller\n#     discards the run. It never prints partial results.\n#   - Writes nothing outside a mktemp dir that is removed on exit. HOME may be\n#     unwritable. It holds no GitHub token and needs none.\n#   - stderr is the job log: tool versions, one line per Go module, final counts.\n#\n# What it does: runs golangci-lint v2 once per go.mod (the repo's own config, or\n# ./golangci.yml next to this script when that human-owned file exists), lists\n# every //nolint directive in .go files, and drops findings whose fingerprint is\n# in the human-owned ./baseline file. A missing baseline fails the run: commit an\n# empty file to mean \"no baseline\".\n#\n# Arguments: none, or exactly --baseline, which prints a baseline of ALL current\n# findings (ignoring ./baseline, not requiring it): scan --baseline > baseline.\n#\n# The golangci-lint flags below are forced after any config, so a repo config\n# cannot truncate output or report \"new issues only\": either would make findings\n# vanish and be autoclosed. Go only, with the image's Go (GOTOOLCHAIN=local).\n#\n# Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 a required tool is missing.\nset -eu\n\ndir=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\n\ndie() { echo \"lint: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }\nneed() { command -v \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"lint: $1 not found\" >&2; exit 2; }; }\n\nmode=findings\ncase $# in\n  0) ;;\n  1) if [ \"$1\" = \"--baseline\" ]; then mode=baseline; else echo \"usage: scan [--baseline]\" >&2; exit 1; fi ;;\n  *) echo \"usage: scan [--baseline]\" >&2; exit 1 ;;\nesac\n\nneed golangci-lint\nneed go\nneed jq\nneed find\nneed grep\n\ntmp=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/ard-lint.XXXXXX\")\n# Go's module cache is read-only on disk; make it removable first.\ncleanup() { chmod -R u+w \"$tmp\" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf \"$tmp\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT\ntrap 'exit 130' INT\ntrap 'exit 143' TERM\n\n# Keep Go's caches off an unwritable HOME and out of the worktree.\nfor v in GOCACHE GOMODCACHE GOPATH; do\n  eval \"cur=\\${$v:-}\"\n  if [ -z \"$cur\" ] || [ ! -w \"$cur\" ]; then\n    eval \"$v=\\$tmp/$v; export $v\"\n  fi\ndone\nGOLANGCI_LINT_CACHE=$tmp/golangci\nGOWORK=off GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly GOTOOLCHAIN=local\nexport GOLANGCI_LINT_CACHE GOWORK GOFLAGS GOTOOLCHAIN\n\nversion=$(golangci-lint version --short 2>/dev/null || golangci-lint --version | head -n 1) || version=unknown\necho \"golangci-lint: $version\" >&2\necho \"go: $(go env GOVERSION)\" >&2\n\nif [ \"$mode\" = findings ]; then\n  [ -f \"$dir/baseline\" ] || die 'no baseline file: generate one with \"scan --baseline > baseline\" in the role directory and commit it (an empty file means no baseline)'\n  baseline=$dir/baseline\nelse\n  : > \"$tmp/empty\"\n  baseline=$tmp/empty\nfi\n\ncfg=\nif [ -f \"$dir/golangci.yml\" ]; then\n  cfg=\"--config $dir/golangci.yml\"\n  echo \"golangci: using role config\" >&2\nelse\n  echo \"golangci: repo config or defaults\" >&2\nfi\n\nprune='( -name .git -o -name vendor -o -name node_modules -o -name testdata ) -prune'\n\n# golangci-lint, once per Go module. Fail closed: a module that cannot be\n# analysed fails the run.\n: > \"$tmp/gl.jsonl\"\nfind . $prune -o -name go.mod -type f -print > \"$tmp/mods.raw\" || die \"find failed\"\nLC_ALL=C sort \"$tmp/mods.raw\" > \"$tmp/mods.txt\"\nn=0\nwhile IFS= read -r f; do\n  manifest=${f#./}\n  mdir=$(dirname -- \"$manifest\")\n  n=$((n + 1))\n  rc=0\n  # $cfg is intentionally unquoted: it is empty or two words.\n  # shellcheck disable=SC2086\n  (cd -- \"$mdir\" && golangci-lint run $cfg \\\n    --path-mode=abs --output.json.path=\"$tmp/$n.json\" --output.text.path=stderr \\\n    --show-stats=false --issues-exit-code=0 --max-issues-per-linter=0 --max-same-issues=0 \\\n    --new=false --new-from-rev= --new-from-merge-base= --new-from-patch= \\\n    --fix=false --allow-parallel-runners ./...) 2>\"$tmp/gl.err\" || rc=$?\n  if [ \"$rc\" -ne 0 ]; then\n    if grep -qi 'go version\\|requires go\\|toolchain' \"$tmp/gl.err\"; then\n      tail -n 3 \"$tmp/gl.err\" >&2\n      die \"$manifest needs a newer Go than the image's $(go env GOVERSION); update the lint image\"\n    fi\n    die \"golangci-lint failed in $manifest (exit $rc): $(tail -n 3 \"$tmp/gl.err\")\"\n  fi\n  [ -s \"$tmp/$n.json\" ] || die \"golangci-lint wrote no report for $manifest\"\n  jq -c --arg module \"$mdir\" '{module: $module, report: .}' \"$tmp/$n.json\" >> \"$tmp/gl.jsonl\" \\\n    || die \"cannot parse golangci-lint output for $manifest\"\n  echo \"golangci-lint: $manifest: $(jq '(.Issues // []) | length' \"$tmp/$n.json\") issue(s)\" >&2\ndone < \"$tmp/mods.txt\"\n\n# //nolint directives are findings: they hide linter output.\n: > \"$tmp/nolint.jsonl\"\nrc=0\nfind . $prune -o -name '*.go' -type f -exec grep -lE '//[[:space:]]*nolint' {} + > \"$tmp/nolint.files\" || rc=$?\n[ \"$rc\" -le 1 ] || die \"searching for nolint directives failed\"\nLC_ALL=C sort \"$tmp/nolint.files\" > \"$tmp/nolint.sorted\"\nwhile IFS= read -r f; do\n  grep -nE '//[[:space:]]*nolint' \"$f\" \\\n    | jq -R -c --arg path \"${f#./}\" 'capture(\"^(?<line>[0-9]+):(?<text>.*)$\") | {path: $path, line: (.line|tonumber), text}' \\\n    >> \"$tmp/nolint.jsonl\" || die \"cannot read nolint directives in $f\"\ndone < \"$tmp/nolint.sorted\"\n\n# Merge. golangci-lint (--path-mode=abs) uses absolute paths; strip either root.\nroot=$(pwd -P)\nlroot=$(pwd)\nrun_jq() {\n  jq -n \"$1\" --arg mode \"$2\" --arg root \"$root\" --arg lroot \"$lroot\" --arg version \"$version\" \\\n    --rawfile baseline \"$baseline\" --slurpfile gl \"$tmp/gl.jsonl\" --slurpfile nolint \"$tmp/nolint.jsonl\" \\\n    -f \"$dir/normalize.jq\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$mode\" = baseline ]; then\n  run_jq -r baseline > \"$tmp/out\" || die \"normalize failed\"\n  echo \"lint: baseline written\" >&2\n  cat \"$tmp/out\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n\nrun_jq -c findings > \"$tmp/out\" || die \"normalize failed\"\nrun_jq -r fingerprints > \"$tmp/fps.raw\" || die \"normalize failed\"\nLC_ALL=C sort -u \"$tmp/fps.raw\" > \"$tmp/fps\"\nsed -e 's/\\r$//' -e 's/^[[:space:]]*//' -e 's/[[:space:]]*$//' \"$baseline\" \\\n  | grep -v -e '^#' -e '^$' | LC_ALL=C sort -u > \"$tmp/base\" || true\ncount=$(wc -l < \"$tmp/out\" | tr -d ' ')\nbaselined=$(LC_ALL=C comm -12 \"$tmp/fps\" \"$tmp/base\" | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\nunused=$(LC_ALL=C comm -13 \"$tmp/fps\" \"$tmp/base\" | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\necho \"lint: $count finding(s), $baselined baselined, $unused baseline entries unused\" >&2\ncat \"$tmp/out\"\ndiff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile\nindex 1dd6ab8..7c4f294 100644\n--- a/Makefile\n+++ b/Makefile\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n VERSION ?= $(shell git describe --tags --always --dirty 2>/dev/null || echo dev)\n LDFLAGS := -s -w -X main.version=$(VERSION)\n \n-.PHONY: build test lint fmt clean cve-fixtures chart-test image-test\n+.PHONY: build test lint fmt clean cve-fixtures lint-scanner-fixtures chart-test image-test\n \n build:\n \tCGO_ENABLED=0 go build -ldflags \"$(LDFLAGS)\" -o bin/ard ./cmd/ard\n@@ -33,5 +33,12 @@ cve-fixtures:\n \tdocker run --rm --user \"$$(id -u):$$(id -g)\" -e HOME=/tmp \\\n \t  -v \"$$PWD/internal/roles:/roles\" -w /roles ard-cve-fixtures sh testdata/cve/regen.sh\n \n+# Regenerates the real lint scanner fixtures in the pinned image (see\n+# internal/roles/testdata/lint/regen.sh). Needs Docker; not part of `make test`.\n+lint-scanner-fixtures:\n+\tdocker build -t ard-lint-fixtures internal/roles/scanners/lint\n+\tdocker run --rm --user \"$$(id -u):$$(id -g)\" -e HOME=/tmp \\\n+\t  -v \"$$PWD/internal/roles:/roles\" -w /roles ard-lint-fixtures sh testdata/lint/regen.sh\n+\n clean:\n \trm -rf bin\ndiff --git a/internal/initcmd/body.go b/internal/initcmd/body.go\nindex b9fea42..dab52be 100644\n--- a/internal/initcmd/body.go\n+++ b/internal/initcmd/body.go\n@@ -30,6 +30,12